Subject: net: resolve names through the WASIX runtime with the wasix build tag
Last-Update: 2026-10-04

The cgo resolver's entry points are implemented over WASIX's resolve
call, which answers from the runtime's resolver, so a program needs
neither /etc/resolv.conf nor a UDP socket to look up a name. wasip1
prefers it whenever it is available, as Windows and Android prefer
theirs. The runtime resolves names to addresses only: a port lookup
reports the port unknown, as a resolver reports one it does not find,
and the package reads its own table; a canonical-name lookup reports
that the runtime does not offer it and the package asks DNS; and a
reverse lookup fails.

